  "dataCard": {},
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10a-catfishes-corydoras-co/unusual_ornamental_fish_bred_in_indonesia_2_corydoras_septentrionalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Corydoras septentrionalis is rather rare in the trade. It is very similar to Corydoras ellisae from Paraguay. It differs from C. ellisae mainly by its much longer snout and its colourless fins (with a spotted pattern in C. ellisae).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10a-catfishes-corydoras-co/unusual_ornamental_fish_bred_in_indonesia_2_corydoras_septentrionalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Corydoras septentrionalis occurs in Venezuela and Colombia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10a-catfishes-corydoras-co/unusual_ornamental_fish_bred_in_indonesia_2_corydoras_septentrionalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Few Corydoras species show such fascinating behaviour. When males compete with each other, or when the winner of the competition courts the female, the proceedings are so fast that the eye can hardly follow.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10a-catfishes-corydoras-co/unusual_ornamental_fish_bred_in_indonesia_2_corydoras_septentrionalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species has a very nice metallic green shine on the body when the light falls in the right way. Specimens bred in Indonesia are available.</p>"
    }
  ],
